WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.200
-Hello and welcome,
welcome, welcome, welcome

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:04.200
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:05.534
You're here.
Thank you very much.

00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:07.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:08.567
Welcome. Thank you for watching.

00:00:08.567 --> 00:00:09.868
Well, guys, last night,

00:00:09.868 --> 00:00:12.767
President Biden hosted
the president of South Korea

00:00:12.767 --> 00:00:14.501
for a White House state dinner.

00:00:14.501 --> 00:00:15.701
And the South Korean president

00:00:15.701 --> 00:00:18.734
actually sang a rendition
of his favorite song.

00:00:18.734 --> 00:00:19.767
Watch this.

00:00:19.767 --> 00:00:22.834
-♪ A long, long time ago ♪

00:00:24.968 --> 00:00:33.100
♪ I can still remember how that
music used to make me smile ♪

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:42.334
♪ Something touched me deep
inside the day the music died ♪

00:00:42.334 --> 00:00:44.300
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Oh!

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:51.300
-Wow! That's actually...

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:52.667
There's always that
one friend at karaoke

00:00:52.667 --> 00:00:55.067
who knows they're good,
you know?

00:00:55.067 --> 00:00:56.400
"I don't need the lyrics.
I don't need the..."

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:59.000
♪ Don't stop, belie-- ♪

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:00.234
Meanwhile, this morning,

00:01:00.234 --> 00:01:01.834
the president of South Korea
woke up like,

00:01:01.834 --> 00:01:04.767
"I did what last night?

00:01:04.767 --> 00:01:07.200
Honey, you got to get me out
of there when I get like that."

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.701
You know, this actually
reminds me of the time

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:11.133
another world leader
did something similar.

00:01:11.133 --> 00:01:14.501
-Mommy don't know
that daddy's getting hot.

00:01:14.501 --> 00:01:16.367
At the body shop.

00:01:16.367 --> 00:01:18.367
Doing something unholy.

00:01:18.367 --> 00:01:21.501
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Remember that?

00:01:21.501 --> 00:01:23.067
-Ike?!

00:01:24.334 --> 00:01:26.534
-Meanwhile, yesterday,
Biden told reporters that

00:01:26.534 --> 00:01:29.067
before he decided to run
for re-election,

00:01:29.067 --> 00:01:31.467
he took a hard look
at his age.

00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:34.767
Is it me or does Biden
always look like

00:01:34.767 --> 00:01:35.934
he's taking a hard look?

00:01:35.934 --> 00:01:37.200
You know, he's always like...

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:47.334
Then Biden reminded everyone
that he's the same age

00:01:47.334 --> 00:01:50.100
as Lincoln...if he
were still alive today.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:54.634
Some more news from
The White House.

00:01:54.634 --> 00:01:56.801
Today, for
Take Your Child to Work Day,

00:01:56.801 --> 00:01:59.501
Biden held an event
with his staffers' kids.

00:01:59.501 --> 00:02:02.100
Yep, Biden spent time with
White House staffers' kids.

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:03.868
He even took
some questions from them.

00:02:03.868 --> 00:02:04.868
Let's see how that went.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:15.834
-One granddaughter lives
in -- in Pennsylvania,

00:02:15.834 --> 00:02:17.667
in Philadelphia.

00:02:17.667 --> 00:02:20.868
One granddaughter
lives in New York.

00:02:20.868 --> 00:02:23.567
One granddaughter
lives in Washington.

00:02:23.567 --> 00:02:25.434
One granddaughter
lives in Wilmington.

00:02:25.434 --> 00:02:28.133
My grandson lives in California.

00:02:28.133 --> 00:02:30.501
I left somebody out, didn't I?
Anyway...

00:02:31.434 --> 00:02:33.868
I did say five. You're right.
So, let me see.

00:02:33.868 --> 00:02:38.000
I got two in Philadelphia.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:40.400
They're confusing me.
But they're all around.

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:42.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.868 --> 00:02:48.067
-The kid was like,
"You might want to take

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:51.133
a harder look
at that age thing, you know?"

00:02:51.133 --> 00:02:52.167
Then Biden looked
at the kid like,

00:02:52.167 --> 00:02:53.200
"Hey, what is this?

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:54.601
'Meet the Press'?
Cut me some slack."

00:02:54.601 --> 00:02:56.000
You know you only said five?

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:58.300
Anyway, long story short,
that kid's parent was fired.

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:00.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.234
Yeah, there you go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:08.467 --> 00:03:11.033
"I got one grandkid who lives
in Pennsylvania.

00:03:11.033 --> 00:03:12.300
One..."

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:13.968
My goodness.

00:03:13.968 --> 00:03:15.701
Other kids are like,
"Hey, come on.

00:03:15.701 --> 00:03:17.801
We got questions, too, man.

00:03:17.801 --> 00:03:20.501
What's your favorite ice cream?!
Come on!"

00:03:20.501 --> 00:03:21.767
You guys see this?

00:03:21.767 --> 00:03:24.400
Last night, Tucker Carlson
posted a video on Twitter

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:25.901
where he spoke out
for the first time

00:03:25.901 --> 00:03:27.234
since his exit from Fox News.

00:03:27.234 --> 00:03:28.367
Take a look at this.

00:03:28.367 --> 00:03:29.701
-One of the first things
you realize

00:03:29.701 --> 00:03:32.267
when you step
outside the noise for a few days

00:03:32.267 --> 00:03:35.000
is how many genuinely
nice people there are.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:36.968
The other thing you notice
when you take a little time off

00:03:36.968 --> 00:03:40.968
is how unbelievably stupid
most of the debates you see

00:03:40.968 --> 00:03:42.400
on television are.

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:44.734
-Yeah. Nothing says
"I landed on my feet"

00:03:44.734 --> 00:03:47.334
like ranting
in a decommissioned sauna.

00:03:50.567 --> 00:03:52.467
He stood up,
he's wearing a towel.

00:03:52.467 --> 00:03:54.834
He's like, "Alright."

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:56.868
Yep, Tucker criticized
the current state of debate

00:03:56.868 --> 00:03:58.167
on television, then said,

00:03:58.167 --> 00:04:01.801
"And that's why
I chose to be fired."

00:04:01.801 --> 00:04:04.200
I heard that, next month,
Florida Governor Ron DeSantis

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:07.901
plans to launch his
2024 presidential campaign.

00:04:07.901 --> 00:04:10.033
Which makes sense because,
already, his campaign

00:04:10.033 --> 00:04:13.567
slogan is "Mayday, Mayday."

00:04:13.567 --> 00:04:15.901
Yeah, DeSantis is having
a tough time.

00:04:15.901 --> 00:04:17.968
It's hard to say you'd work
well with other countries

00:04:17.968 --> 00:04:19.868
when you can't even
get along with Epcot.

00:04:19.868 --> 00:04:22.767
You know what I'm saying?

00:04:22.767 --> 00:04:25.734
Speaking of Disney,
this is going viral.

00:04:25.734 --> 00:04:27.667
Disney released posters
for each character

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:29.968
in their new live-action
"Little Mermaid" movie,

00:04:29.968 --> 00:04:33.467
and people think Flounder
looks a little too realistic.

00:04:33.467 --> 00:04:35.133
Check it out.
Here's the original Flounder.

00:04:35.133 --> 00:04:36.801
Now here's the new one.

00:04:36.801 --> 00:04:39.300
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:42.334
Well, I guess Disney wants
all the ocean characters

00:04:42.334 --> 00:04:43.367
to be super-accurate.

00:04:43.367 --> 00:04:45.200
I mean, look at this teaser
I saw.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:48.601
-The Magical World of Disney
invites you under the sea,

00:04:48.601 --> 00:04:51.701
where you'll meet
Sebastian, Scuttle,

00:04:51.701 --> 00:04:54.968
flounder, and an
all-new ocean character,

00:04:54.968 --> 00:04:56.567
Dirk.
-[ Coughs ]

00:04:56.567 --> 00:04:58.234
-The [bleep] you looking at?

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:05.234
-Wow! That is real.

00:05:06.167 --> 00:05:07.534
-Wow!

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:10.434
-Hey, I read that,
according to a sleep expert,

00:05:10.434 --> 00:05:11.601
if you want
a good night's rest,

00:05:11.601 --> 00:05:14.901
your bedroom should be
stark and bare.

00:05:14.901 --> 00:05:16.634
Yep. So, apparently, the best
place to sleep is

00:05:16.634 --> 00:05:18.300
Bed Bath &amp; Beyond.

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:21.501
Oh!
-Oh, hey! Oh!

00:05:21.501 --> 00:05:23.334
Hey! Hey!
-Wow!

00:05:23.334 --> 00:05:25.300
-Oh, hey! Hey!
-Wow!

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:27.501
-Finally, guys, I was
watching TV the other day.

00:05:27.501 --> 00:05:28.667
I was just flipping
through the channels

00:05:28.667 --> 00:05:31.567
and I came across
this show on TeenNick.

00:05:31.567 --> 00:05:33.133
It's called "Ew!"

00:05:33.133 --> 00:05:34.601
And it's a pretty good show.

00:05:34.601 --> 00:05:37.033
And a lot of people say that
I look like the main character.

00:05:37.033 --> 00:05:38.200
I don't know
if I see it, though.

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:39.734
But, anyways, here,
look for yourselves.

00:05:39.734 --> 00:05:41.834
Here's the latest
episode of "Ew!"

00:05:41.834 --> 00:05:43.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:43.234 --> 00:05:49.167
♪♪

00:05:49.167 --> 00:05:51.133
Hi, everyone!

00:05:51.133 --> 00:05:54.634
Welcome to "Ew!"
My name is Sara.

00:05:54.634 --> 00:05:57.834
And if you're wondering,
that's S-A-R-A with no "H,"

00:05:57.834 --> 00:05:59.968
because H's are ew!

00:06:01.567 --> 00:06:04.334
Joining me today is the
new foreign exchange student

00:06:04.334 --> 00:06:07.801
who just moved in across
the street, Bjergen Kjergen.

00:06:07.801 --> 00:06:09.033
Hi, Bjergen.

00:06:09.033 --> 00:06:12.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:12.334 --> 00:06:13.901
Hi, Bjergen.

00:06:13.901 --> 00:06:15.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:19.334 --> 00:06:22.167
-[ Swedish accent ] Hi!
-Hi. How's it going?

00:06:22.167 --> 00:06:25.901
-Pretty good, yeah.
It's great to be on you.

00:06:25.901 --> 00:06:29.767
-Yeah. I love your pigtails.
Did you braid them yourself?

00:06:29.767 --> 00:06:32.534
-No. They were done by
my sisters,

00:06:32.534 --> 00:06:35.200
Herdie, Kerdie, and Donna.

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:37.667
-Yeah. Well, they look amazing.

00:06:37.667 --> 00:06:40.501
So, Bjergen, are you ready for
the school dance competition

00:06:40.501 --> 00:06:41.567
next week?

00:06:41.567 --> 00:06:43.200
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:46.434
But I'm also a bit nervous,
you know?

00:06:46.434 --> 00:06:50.000
I've never danced in front
of other people before.

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:52.167
-Ew! Don't be shy. It's easy.

00:06:52.167 --> 00:06:55.367
We can practice
the dance together right now.

00:06:55.367 --> 00:06:57.534
I'm going to put it on TikTok.

00:06:59.934 --> 00:07:02.634
-♪ You turn me on
like a light switch ♪

00:07:02.634 --> 00:07:05.801
♪ When you're movin' your body
around and around ♪

00:07:05.801 --> 00:07:08.000
♪ Now, I don't wanna
fight this ♪

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:10.234
